MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_001: Apologies that I kept you waiting, Promised One.\nLet's go meet up with the soldiers and train.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_002: <NCA>"You're all scraped up."
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_003: Oh, these? Nothing to worry about. They're mostly\nold scars.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_004: Wounds from battles long ago. I hardly feel them\nanymore.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_005: <NCA>"You're a seasoned hero."
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_006: <NCB>"Try not to overdo it."
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_007: <ACA>Certainly, I have had my fair share of injuries.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_008: <ACB>As I said, don't worry. Every scar marks years of\nexperience in battle.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_009: That said, I have never seen a war like this.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_010: The word "war" hardly seems to capture its scale.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_011: This is not a fight between countries, but between\nhumans and the dead.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_012: <NCA>"It's certainly unusual."
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_013: Yes. An old goat like me can hardly comprehend\nall of it. Not that that's a first for me.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_014: In the past decade I have encountered many a\nsituation that tested my every belief.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_015: I lost the person I loved and respected most.\nLady Leda was caught up in a staggering conspiracy.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_016: You know, I was once a servant of the temple who\nearned the rank of pilus prior in the empire's army.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_017: That man could scarcely dream that he would see\nthe world so changed.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_018: Oh...
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_019: The scars don't pain me. What hurts is the harrowing\nsense that the ground is shaking beneath me.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_020: I cannot pray to the gods, and I cannot pray to\nthe dead. What is there left to put faith in?
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_021: <NCA>"Why not put faith in me?"
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_022: Huh. I wouldn't have thought someone with a grand\ntitle like yours would go around asking politely.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_023: Heh. It's like the day that I decided to serve\nLord Guillermo.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_024: I had drawn my sword and challenged him, and he\nbrought me to my knees...
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_025: and then asked me to follow him. I could not help\nbut smile at his generosity.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_026: Up until now, I'd chalked up the people's faith in you\nas a simple need for guidance.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_A_027: But yes... I, too, will put faith in you, Promised One.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_S: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_S_001: Once again, I find myself alone.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_S_002: You saved the world as I believed you would—but at\nthe cost of your own life. I can't bear it!
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_S_003: <NCA>"Buccar."
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_S_004: You're alive!
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_S_005: Oh, thank goodness.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_S_006: <NCA>"You've been waiting?"
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_S_007: <NCB>"I'm sorry if I worried you."
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_S_008: <ACA>No. Apologies, but I'm here for another reason.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_S_009: <ACB>You misunderstand. I wasn't here praying for\nyour safety.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_S_010: I came here to atone.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_S_011: When you vanished, I assumed I had survived in\nplace of others I cared about...again.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_S_012: It was much like the day I lost Lord Guillermo and\nmy countrymen in Cydonia. I felt I carried the blame.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_S_013: Seeing your face, I feel I've been saved.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_S_014: Thank you... Thank you for coming back.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_S_015: <NCA>"I'm glad you're safe too."
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_S_016: You're generous to care about a lowly man like me.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_S_017: So very generous...
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_S_018: <NCA>"You could at least smile."
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_S_019: You want to see me smile? I must say, that's\nsomething of a rarity.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_S_020: Since losing Lord Guillermo, I stopped smiling as I\ndid in the old days.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_S_021: <RSDS>But I do feel cheerful now. Indeed, whenever I'm\nwith you, Promised One, my heart feels light.
MID_SE_Ism_Buc_S_022: I can smile again with you.